      "text": "To find the distance between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) in a coordinate plane, we use the distance formula:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nGiven the points \\((-3, -4)\\) and \\((4, -5)\\), we can substitute \\(x_1 = -3\\), \\(y_1 = -4\\), \\(x_2 = 4\\), and \\(y_2 = -5\\) into the formula:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(4 - (-3))^2 + (-5 - (-4))^2}\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expressions inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(4 + 3)^2 + (-5 + 4)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{7^2 + (-1)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{49 + 1}\n\\]\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{50}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify \\(\\sqrt{50}\\), we recognize that \\(50 = 25 \\times 2\\):\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{50} = \\sqrt{25 \\times 2} = \\sqrt{25} \\times \\sqrt{2} = 5\\sqrt{2}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance between the points \\((-3, -4)\\) and \\((4, -5)\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5\\sqrt{2}}\n\\]",
